"use strict";

/* generated from story/scenes/act3_ch15.md — do not edit */

SC["a3c15_clearwater"]={t:()=>SYS(`CHAPTER FIFTEEN — THE SECOND FURNACE`)+P(`Clearwater Hall is, and this is the part that takes getting used to, <i>nice</i>.`)+P(`A modest river sect on a willow-hung shore: three courtyards, a famous meditation hall, a school that teaches boatmen's children their characters for free. Its disciples are mediocre and cheerful. Its servants are paid on time, fed from the same pot as the masters, and speak of the place the way people speak of a kind uncle. The town loves it. The fish practically jump into its nets. Clearwater Hall is prosperous, beloved, and gentle, and it has been all three for forty years, and you know exactly what forty years of unearned gentleness costs, and who pays it, because you've read the receipts.`)+((G.f.a3_route=="sect")?(P(`The writ opens every door. <i>Itinerant auditor of the Azure Cloud</i> — the abbot himself receives you, a soft-handed old man with a smile like warmed oil, delighted, honored, eager to show the books. The books are perfect. That's its own answer: nobody's real books are perfect.`)):(P(`You come in the servants' way, hired off the dock to haul for the kitchens — and the basement's freemasonry takes you in by sundown, soup and gossip and all. Everything the servants say about the hall is kind. Everything. Forty years and not one grievance worth a whisper. You've lived in a basement; you know what a scrubbed ledger sounds like.`)))+P(`Under it all, beneath the meditation hall, where only you can hear it: a hum. Familiar as a scar. Patient as interest.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Find a way down.`,go:"a3c15_under"}]};

SC["a3c15_under"]={img:"shrine",
 t:()=>P(`It takes three nights to find the way in — a maintenance stair behind the meditation hall's altar, worn smooth by forty years of one pair of slippers — and what's at the bottom is Kang's hall in miniature, tended like a shrine.`)+P(`A loom the size of a millstone. A pit of black iron, banked and warm. Soul-threads stretched across it — nine on the frame now, faded gold, each one once a person who washed up on a riverbank confused and far from home — and a tenth bracket, empty, polished, <i>ready</i>. Nine at a time is all the frame holds; the spent ones go downriver, and the schedule on the wall counts the going in a merchant's neat hand: the silkworm seal, season by season, four decades of receipts. And one line that changes the shape of the war: <i>inspection — autumn, as customary.</i>`)+P(`The Court doesn't just collect. It <i>visits</i>. Franchises have inspectors, and autumn is six weeks out.`)+((G.insight>=9)?(P(`You read the loom's feeding rhythm the way Qiu's ledger taught you to read skims: the pit is banked to a schedule, and the schedule says the empty bracket isn't decoration. Someone is meant to fill it before the inspection — a gift laid out for the inspector's arrival, a duck fattened for a festival. Someone in this kind, gentle hall has already been chosen.`)):("")),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`The abbot's slippers are on the stair behind you.`,do:()=>{if(G.insight>=9)G.f.a3_schedule=true;},go:"a3c15_choice"}]};

SC["a3c15_choice"]={t:()=>P(`The abbot doesn't call for guards. That's the worst of it. He sits down on the bottom stair like a tired grandfather and explains, gently, patiently, the way he'd teach a boatman's child their characters: the flood-wards, the healing hall, the free school, the forty years of nobody in this town going hungry — all of it paid for by nine souls who fell out of the sky owing this world nothing. “They were nobody's,” he says, without cruelty, which is somehow worse than cruelty. “And they made ten thousand somebodies safe. I'll show you the arithmetic, auditor. It balances.”`)+P(`It does balance. You've checked. That's never once been the question.`)+P(`Six weeks until the inspector. Nine threads on the loom, one bracket empty, and a choice the whole act has been walking toward:`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Free it NOW. Tonight. Nine souls don't spend six more weeks as firewood for anyone's strategy.`,go:"a3c15_free"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Document everything, reset the stair-dust, and WAIT for the inspector. You came for the Court, not its kindest franchise.`,do:()=>{addIns(1);},go:"a3c15_wait"}]};

SC["a3c15_free"]={t:()=>P(`You do it that night, and it is easier than Kang's hall by a mile — nine threads, a banked pit, a tender instead of a warlord — and that easiness should have warned you.`)+P(`The threads come free one by one, keening, rising through the meditation hall's roof-vents into the dark, nine souls going home or onward, and the hum under Clearwater Hall stops for the first time in forty years. The town will start paying for its own flood-wards now. The school will start charging. The arithmetic you broke was real, and the town will feel it for a generation, and you stand in the dead shrine certain, not comfortable — there's a difference, and tonight is when you learn it.`)+P(`But the abbot is gone. Slippers, ledger-copy, riverboat — gone upriver-by-dark toward the lake country with forty years of habit and one fresh terror, and you know exactly where a frightened franchisee runs: to the franchise.`)+SYS(`The Court will know you're coming.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Follow. The marshes between here and the lake country have been whispering about something anyway.`,do:()=>{G.f.a3_warned=true;G.f.a3_furnace="freed";},go:"a3c16_marsh"}]};

SC["a3c15_wait"]={t:()=>P(`You close the stair behind you, reset the dust with a tracer-thread only you could see was moved, and you wait, and the waiting is the hardest work the basement ever trained you for.`)+P(`You document everything: the schedule, the seal, the loom's knots, the abbot's rounds, rubbings of forty years of receipts. You haul kitchen loads. You're pleasant. And on the ninth night, the hum under the meditation hall changes key: deeper, the sound of a pot with something new in it. You stand in the servants' dormitory with your jaw locked, doing the arithmetic awake: the tenth bracket. Filled, partially, on schedule — a beggar, the kitchen whispers next morning, a riverbank drifter nobody's, fed warm meals at the gate for a month prior. <i>Fattened.</i>`)+P(`Not dead — the feeding takes a season; the inspector arrives in six weeks and you can free a half-fed soul as surely as a whole-spent one. That's what you tell yourself. You hold the line. Every night the hum holds it with you.`)+SYS(`The schedule, the seal, the rubbings — and a cost you chose to watch. Documented.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`The marshes between here and the lake country have been whispering about something. Six weeks is time enough to look.`,do:()=>{G.f.a3_documented=true;G.f.a3_furnace="waiting";},go:"a3c16_marsh"}]};